title: A Letter from Lenin
subtitle: Lenin has written to the German communists.
view-if: congress_jena = 1 and congress_closing = 0 and e21_cg_lenin_out = 0 and comintern_member = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.month_actions += 1;
Q.e21_cg_lenin_out = 1;
Q.e21_lenin_letter_mood = (Q.ecci_lenin >= 60) ? 1 : ((Q.ecci_lenin >= 40) ? 2 : 3);
Q.e21_backing_right = (Q.congress_backing == 'unionist') ? 1 : 0;
Q.sys_outcome = 0;
!}
frequency: 400
is-card: true
new-page: true
tags: congress

= A Letter from Lenin

The letter is dated 14 August and addressed to the congress. It is long and plain. The March Action was a mistake, Lenin writes, and the party must now win the majority of the working class. The Left is to stop hunting Levi's friends, and the Zentrale is to stop looking over its shoulder at the Left.

[? if e21_lenin_letter_mood = 1 : Between the lines, the delegates can read that Lenin trusts the German Zentrale. ?][? if e21_lenin_letter_mood = 2 : Lenin is careful to praise no one by name. ?][? if e21_lenin_letter_mood = 3 : Lenin does not mention the German Zentrale at all, and everybody notices. ?] [? if e21_backing_right = 1 : It reads like a speech for our motion. ?][? if e21_backing_right = 0 : It reads like a speech for the Right's motion. ?]

- @read: Read the whole letter to the congress.
- @quote: Quote only the passages that suit us.
- @leave: Have it printed and laid on every seat.

@read
subtitle: [? if lock_moscow_orders = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Lenin's name moves the hall towards the Right, and calms it.
choose-if: lock_moscow_orders < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids taking orders from Moscow, even from Lenin.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_moscow_orders == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 5;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 5;
}
var f = (Q.e21_lenin_letter_mood == 1) ? 0.08 : ((Q.e21_lenin_letter_mood == 2) ? 0.05 : 0.03);
if (Q.unionist_gone != 1) { RG.congress.swayTo('unionist', f); }
RG.congress.bitter(-2);
RG.ecci('lenin', 4);
!}

The chair reads the letter from beginning to end, and the hall is very quiet. [+ congress_last_moved +] delegates who came to Jena to settle accounts decide that Lenin has settled them already.

@quote
subtitle: Works if nobody has read the whole letter. Somebody usually has.
on-arrival: {!
RG.congress.sway(0.05 + Math.random() * 0.03);
if (Math.random() < 0.35) {
    Q.sys_outcome = 2;
    RG.congress.lose(0.04);
    RG.congress.bitter(3);
} else {
    Q.sys_outcome = 1;
}
RG.ecci('lenin', -4);
!}

Our speakers quote Lenin where he agrees with us and pass over the rest. [? if sys_outcome = 1 : [+ congress_last_moved +] delegates come over. ?][? if sys_outcome = 2 : Then a delegate from Thuringia reads out the passages we left out, and we lose friends we had. ?]

@leave
subtitle: Nobody can say we used Lenin's name. The letter does its work slowly.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.unionist_gone != 1) { RG.congress.swayTo('unionist', 0.025); }
Q.independence += 1;
!}

The letter is printed overnight. By the morning session most delegates have read it, and some have changed their minds, mostly towards the Right.
